- op: update  # 376c
  at: '2026-05-14T19:53:02Z'  # 376c
  by: agent  # 376c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 376c
  clock: 3  # 376c
  nonce: 376c  # 376c
  set:  # 376c
    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per discussion in conversation surrounding WI-votut (`.csv.erb` extension fix). The docstring of `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/view_template.py:30` claims `Future: Django, Laravel, Phoenix, Spring`, but no convention-based template-binding linker exists for any framework other than Rails. `view_template.py:279` is the only producer of `renders` edges in the entire codebase.\n\n## Gap\n\n`hypergumbo run` on a Django app produces no `renders` edge connecting a view function/class to its template file. The implicit `render(request, \"<template>.html\", ctx)` → `<app>/templates/<app>/<template>.html` relationship is not captured.\n\n## Django convention to model\n\n- **Action detection**: function-based views (FBVs — any function on `urls.py`-imported module that takes `(request, ...)`) and class-based views (CBVs — methods `get`/`post`/`put`/`delete`/`patch`/`head`/`options` on subclasses of `View` and friends).\n- **Base classes**: `View`, `TemplateView`, `ListView`, `DetailView`, `CreateView`, `UpdateView`, `DeleteView`, `RedirectView`.\n- **Template path derivation**:\n  - Explicit-string strategy: `render(request, \"users/show.html\", ctx)` → `templates/users/show.html` or `<app>/templates/users/show.html`.\n  - Class-attribute variant of explicit-string strategy: `TemplateView.template_name = \"users/show.html\"` → same.\n  - Method/class-name strategy: DetailView/ListView default → `<app>/<model>_detail.html` / `<app>/<model>_list.html`.\n- **Extensions**: `.html`, `.jinja`, `.j2`, `.html.djinja`.\n\n## First-framework responsibility (extract shared core during this PR)\n\nThis PR is also responsible for extracting the probe-and-emit core from `view_template.py` into a shared module (suggested name: `view_template_core.py` or `_view_template_core.py`). The Rails-specific code becomes a thin strategy. The shared core handles the filesystem probe loop, `renders` edge emission (`evidence_type=naming_convention`, `confidence=0.85`, `detection_pattern=implicit_convention`), and template Symbol creation.\n\n**The shared core MUST support two strategy classes from day one.** This scope is load-bearing for the sister items WI-dajom/WI-hogik/WI-hokaj:\n\n1. **Method/class-name strategy** — the action's name (and surrounding class/module) derives the template path. Rails (existing), Phoenix (WI-dajom), and Django CBV defaults all use this shape.\n2. **Explicit-string strategy** — the template path is the literal string argument to a render-style call, or a class-attribute string literal. Django `render(request, \"...\")` and `TemplateView.template_name = \"...\"` already exercise this; Spring (WI-hogik) and Laravel (WI-hokaj) depend on it.\n\nSetting up both strategy hooks in this PR avoids forcing Spring/Laravel to refactor the core later. If for some reason only one strategy ships here, document explicitly which sister item is then responsible for extracting the second.\n\n## Sister items (build against the extracted core)\n\n- WI-dajom (Phoenix) — method-name strategy.\n- WI-hogik (Spring MVC) — explicit-string strategy (string return value).\n- WI-hokaj (Laravel Blade) — explicit-string strategy (string arg to `view()` call).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A Django fixture with `urls.py` → `views.py` → `templates/<app>/<name>.html` produces a `renders` edge from the view function to the template file (explicit-string strategy via `render(...)`).\n- `TemplateView.template_name = \"...\"` produces a `renders` edge (class-attribute variant of explicit-string strategy).\n- DetailView / ListView with model-derived defaults produce `renders` edges (method/class-name strategy).\n- The shared core exposes both `MethodNameStrategy` and `ExplicitStringStrategy` (or equivalent) hooks; existing Rails behavior is implemented as a `MethodNameStrategy` subclass.\n- 100% coverage on changed source; existing 43 Rails tests still pass; existing test_view_template_linker.py refactored against the new shared core.\n\n## Out of scope (for first cut; revisit if corpus demands)\n\n- DRF ViewSets with `renderer_classes` including `TemplateHTMLRenderer` + `template_name`. Rare in practice (DRF is JSON-first); treat as enhancement, not blocker. If the prospector corpus has Django-REST repos that template-render at non-trivial volume, file a separate child item.\n\n## Priority calibration\n\nP3 is conservative. Per AGENTS.md \"Linker subcategory vocabulary and prioritization\" — rank by expected FP-reduction volume on the prospector corpus, not language novelty. If Django repos contribute meaningful dead-code FP volume in the current corpus, this plausibly deserves P2. Worth a quick corpus check before promotion."  # 376c
